"""Morning readings adapted from C. H. Spurgeon, "Morning and Evening" (1866) — public domain.

Translated into Khmer and shortened (not word for word): the long Victorian sentences are made
simple, old English customs are left out, and every verse is shown live from ពគប. The question
and the prayer at the end are added for this site. 5 November uses Spurgeon's evening reading
(the morning one is about English history of 1605/1688).

Built into data/devotionals.json by scripts/build_devos.py. A month's readings are only used
(website + Facebook/Telegram) after its number is added to "approved" at the very start of
data/devotionals.json, e.g.  {"approved":["11"], ...   — please have a pastor read them first.

Fields: (MM-DD, id, title, key verse, passage to read, reading, question, prayer)
"""
